{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00231",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 2.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Hello. Right, let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 3.13,
      "end_seconds": 7.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.67,
      "end_seconds": 14.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Alright, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. In your own words, what's happened?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.6,
      "end_seconds": 24.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "I mean, I've been dealing with a red swollen area on my leg. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.11,
      "end_seconds": 30.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "And when did that start? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.96,
      "end_seconds": 33.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "About... well, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.94,
      "end_seconds": 35.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.15,
      "end_seconds": 38.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.31,
      "end_seconds": 43.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 43.91,
      "end_seconds": 49.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.3,
      "end_seconds": 54.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Have you had a fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.55,
      "end_seconds": 57.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.42,
      "end_seconds": 61.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.82,
      "end_seconds": 67.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.11,
      "end_seconds": 73.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.73,
      "end_seconds": 76.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.0,
      "end_seconds": 80.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Have you found anything that eases it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.11,
      "end_seconds": 87.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "It settles a little with paracetamol. Oh, and a small cut that wasn't healing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.24,
      "end_seconds": 90.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.26,
      "end_seconds": 93.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "I, I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 95.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "What about shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.26,
      "end_seconds": 103.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.62,
      "end_seconds": 109.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Any red streaks going up the leg, pus, calf pain or numbness around it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.2,
      "end_seconds": 124.5,
      "duration_seconds": 14.3,
      "text": "No, you know, no red streaks going up the leg, no pus, no calf pain. I did have pain in that area at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.79,
      "end_seconds": 127.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "And vomiting, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.22,
      "end_seconds": 129.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "No, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 130.04,
      "end_seconds": 133.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.67,
      "end_seconds": 141.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.61,
      "end_seconds": 148.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.75,
      "end_seconds": 151.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Uh, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 151.86,
      "end_seconds": 159.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 96 percent, respiratory rate 20, pulse 96. Blood pressure 108 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.08,
      "end_seconds": 164.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Thanks. Right, what about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.84,
      "end_seconds": 167.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.22,
      "end_seconds": 170.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.57,
      "end_seconds": 173.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.59,
      "end_seconds": 176.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.54,
      "end_seconds": 181.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.35,
      "end_seconds": 184.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.85,
      "end_seconds": 193.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.03,
      "end_seconds": 197.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.2,
      "end_seconds": 206.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Alendronate. I take it 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones. I take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 207.03,
      "end_seconds": 215.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the paracetamol was 325 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.73,
      "end_seconds": 218.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.77,
      "end_seconds": 228.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "I mean, I don't think I have it with me. Seretide inhaler. I take it twice a day for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.99,
      "end_seconds": 229.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.25,
      "end_seconds": 235.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I, I was on Asthalin inhaler before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.02,
      "end_seconds": 242.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.37,
      "end_seconds": 265.48,
      "duration_seconds": 22.11,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years. So, I've got thin bones. My family kept telling me to get it checked. Yes, arthritis in my knees. I have asthma, for two years. I just want to get back to normal, really. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.57,
      "end_seconds": 275.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Okay, thin bones, that's already on your record. Good to know. Okay, arthritis in my knees, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.52,
      "end_seconds": 281.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.54,
      "end_seconds": 284.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.88,
      "end_seconds": 286.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.02,
      "end_seconds": 307.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "There's a small scab where the cut was, no pus coming out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.21,
      "end_seconds": 309.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.91,
      "end_seconds": 330.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "The skin on the lower leg is red, warm and swollen, about the size of my palm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.84,
      "end_seconds": 353.01,
      "duration_seconds": 20.17,
      "text": "So, that's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with cellulitis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a deep vein clot, so we'll keep that open. I can't rule out an abscess forming yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.09,
      "end_seconds": 356.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.56,
      "end_seconds": 378.19,
      "duration_seconds": 17.63,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now cellulitis is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do blood tests for infection. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm going to order a wound swab, for infected wound."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.28,
      "end_seconds": 380.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.61,
      "end_seconds": 391.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "I'm prescribing clindamycin, 300 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days. That's for skin infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.91,
      "end_seconds": 393.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.13,
      "end_seconds": 417.67,
      "duration_seconds": 22.54,
      "text": "Keep the leg raised on a pillow when you're sitting. Mark the edge of the redness with a pen so we can see whether it spreads. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.43,
      "end_seconds": 425.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.73,
      "end_seconds": 427.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.41,
      "end_seconds": 436.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the redness spreads or the fever gets higher."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.84,
      "end_seconds": 441.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.21,
      "end_seconds": 445.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.1,
      "end_seconds": 446.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.01,
      "end_seconds": 451.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.76,
      "end_seconds": 456.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.96,
      "end_seconds": 458.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}